From 6a579dcb7539fe69ab0dcbe055444cf0ba536975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a setting to send native Dolby Vision without
 its trims

Some displays show Dolby Vision with washed-out blacks or wrong colours
because of the trims of the metadata, and look right without them: a
projector was fixed by removing the level 2 trims from the RPU with
dovi_tool (a report in the Kodi forum). "Dolby Vision: leave out the
trims" (videoscreen.hadesdvnotrims, System > Display, off by default)
does that in the player: the display is sent no blocks of levels 2 and 8,
nor of level 10, the targets of level 8 (dvbridge_render_send_trims()).
The picture that is sent does not change, and the display maps each scene
from its level 1 range alone, as it does with metadata that has no trims.

Picking another trim target instead is not offered: how a display selects
or interpolates between the trims of its targets is not specified
publicly, so nothing could say what a choice would do.

Native output takes the setting when it starts, with the engine settings
(CDVEngineSettings::trims), and says it in the log. The Dolby Vision page
of the player information says when the trims of the video are left out
(hades.dv.trims), next to the blocks that are not sent.
